  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "The function $f(x)$ is defined below. What is the value of \n${\\int }_{0}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,?$\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}x-9, & x<5 \\\\ \\frac{x}{5}-5, & x\\ge 5\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "By the additive property of the definite integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}(x-9)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{5}^{10}(\\frac{x}{5}-5)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-9x)|}_{0}^{5}+{(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{10}-5x)|}_{5}^{10} \\\\  & =[\\frac{(5)^{2}}{2}-9(5)-\\frac{(0)^{2}}{2}+9(0)]+[\\frac{(10)^{2}}{10}-5(10)-\\frac{(5)^{2}}{10}+5(5)] \\\\  & =[\\frac{25}{2}-45]+[10-50-\\frac{25}{10}+25] \\\\  & =-50.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
